  "id": "methodological-individualism",
  "term": "methodological individualism",
  "definition": "Methodological individualism is an approach to studying cognition that centers explanation on the individual, especially on internal cognitive mechanisms. In the source context, it is contrasted with wider approaches that also include interactions with other people, groups, tools, and the environment.",
